# {{repo}}

Articles for one publication: drafts, metadata, hand-offs and `ci-review` reviews, one folder per article, every round a commit. This repository is private.

The full rules are in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). This page is the short version for a person.

## Layout

- `articles/<slug>/` holds everything for one article. Files are named `<slug>-draft-rN.md`, `<slug>-metadata-rN.md`, `<slug>-handoff-rN.md`, `<slug>-publication-rN.md`, `<slug>-close-out-rN-to-(code|chat)[-vM].md` and `<slug>-review-rN.md`.
- `articles/<slug>/pipeline/` holds the worklist and the run reports. They are for the author.
- `templates/` holds the shapes of those files.
- `instructions/claude-project.md` is pasted at the top of the claude.ai project's instructions. `instructions/publication.md` holds the publication's own drafting rules and belongs to the author.
- `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, `.gitattributes`, `templates/` and `instructions/claude-project.md` are written by `ci-docs init` from the content-intelligence repository. Edit them there, not here.

## The review loop

1. The drafting side commits `<slug>-draft-rN.md` and `<slug>-metadata-rN.md` together (`draft: <slug> rN`).
2. The author runs `ci-review --github <slug>`.
3. `ci-review` commits `<slug>-review-rN.md` to `main` (`review: <slug> rN`), with the worklist and report under `pipeline/`.
4. The drafting side revises with `templates/revise_after_review_prompt.md` and commits round `rN+1`.

Nothing is renamed, overwritten or deleted. A new round is a new file.

## Refreshing the managed files

From a checkout of content-intelligence:

```
uv run ci-docs init --repo {{repo}}
```

It adds what is missing, skips what is identical, replaces a managed file only if nobody has edited it here, and lists the ones that were edited. It never touches `articles/` or `instructions/publication.md`.
